<!--
beet_esp's entry: the host-side scene-push commands, wired as routes over the
capabilities linked into the `beet` binary (`SceneManagementPlugin`). The `beet`
CLI discovers this file by walking up from the cwd and runs one command per
invocation, so from this directory the scene commands target the device.

`BEET_REMOTE_URL` in this directory's `.env` points every command at the device,
so a `--url` is optional:

    beet load scenes/roomba.bsx      # push a `.bsx` scene to the device
    beet run roomba                  # call a route the pushed scene installed
    beet dump                        # print the device's current scene
    beet clear                       # despawn the scene + reset the hardware
    beet reset                       # return the hardware to its resting state

Requires a `beet` built with the scene-management capabilities (this repo's
`just install-cli`).
-->
<Router {(CliServer, ServeOnLoad)}>
	<SceneLoad/>
	<SceneRun/>
	<SceneDump/>
	<SceneClear/>
	<SceneReset/>
</Router>
